What about directly remove the alternative transcripts and just let one isoform per gene?.
I do not know how methylKit does, but I feel that one way or the other certain artifacts are generated. I mean, let's asume that a DM-CpG lies in a genomic regions that is exon for one isoform.1 and intron for isoform.2. It is that DM-CpG counted twice? (one for exon and one for intron?) Or in the case of a gen with 5 isoforms, are the DM-CpG counted 5 times when analyzing the distribution of DM sites in different genomic features?

